% Problem 23. Chace vol. II pl. 46 (photograph XI, register 2), PDF pp. 139-140; Peet pp. 59-60 (pl. H).
No. 23
"'4 '8 '10 '30 '45; Complete as 2/3."
"{11 '4}  {5 '2 '8}  {4 '2}  {1 '2}  {1}"   % red, each beneath its fraction (values in 45ths); no total written
"Therefore '9 '40 is: to be added to it, making 2/3."   % Chace fn 1: the scribe inadvertently added a stroke above the r of hr
"'4 '8 '9 '10 30 '40 '45 '3 making 1"       % 30 for '30; Chace fn 2: "The scribe omitted the fractional dot."
"11 '4  {5 '2 '8}  {5}  {4 '2}  {1 '2}  {1 '8}  {1}  {15}"   % beneath each fraction (values in 45ths), no total written; 11 '4 is black (Peet fn: "11'4 erroneously in black"); Chace fn 3: the '8 after 5 '2 "appears as '4 on Peet's Plate H but is correct in his text"
